  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1204 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nWV imagery indicates a northwest flow aloft prevailing across the \nWestern High Plains downstream of an upper level high centered over \nthe Four Corners Region. Near the surface, a nearly stalled frontal \nboundary extends from extreme southeast Colorado down into western\nOklahoma.\n\nAlthough drier conditions are likely across much of southwest Kansas \ntonight, there are minimal thunderstorm chances (20%) across central \nKansas even with the SREF depicting a weakening north-northwest flow \naloft with the aforementioned upper level high shifting slightly east\nout of the Four Corners Region into the Southern Rockies. Near the\nsurface, prevailing east-southeast upsloping will reinforce pooled\nmoisture north of a quasi-stationary frontal boundary to our south,\nproviding modest instability across central Kansas with MUCAPE values\nupward of 1000-1500 J/kg. With this setup, thunderstorm development\nis expected across western/central Nebraska late afternoon/early\nevening with storms then spreading south-southeast into northern\nKansas overnight, potentially clipping our northeastern zones near\nthe I-70 corridor. This is suggested by a few CAMs while the HREF\nhints at a 10 to 20% probability of 6-hr QPF exceeding 0.1 of an\ninch by early Saturday morning. A similar set up exists Saturday\nnight into early Sunday morning with little change to the larger\nscale pattern.\n\nTemperatures are forecast to remain a little above the seasonal \naverage tonight as prevailing east-southeast upsloping does little\nto modify the air mass across the region. With the HREF pointing to\na 60 to 80% probability of temperatures dropping below 70F across\nmuch of the area to less than a 10% probability of slipping below\n70F in south central Kansas, look for lows mainly in the 60s(F)\novernight with the lower 70s(F) holding on in south central Kansas.\nHigh temperatures back off a little Saturday with prevailing easterlies\ndrawing in slightly cooler air into western Kansas, lowering H85\ntemperatures down into the mid-20s(C) in central Kansas to the upper\n20s(C) in extreme southwest Kansas. Expect afternoon highs generally\nup into the 90s(F) with the NBM painting a 50 to 70% probability of\ntemperatures exceeding 90F in west central/central Kansas to only\na 60 to 80% probability of temperatures even topping 95F in southwest\nKansas into south central Kansas. Similar highs are expected Sunday.",
